## abzmyan

This project uses **abzmyan**, an optional spec-driven ticket workflow. `.abzmyan/index/` (architecture.md, domain-model.md, api-index.md, tech-stack.md, flow-diagrams.md) is a maintained snapshot of the project's architecture, domain model, and API surface — useful context for non-trivial work, but you don't need it for questions or small edits.

Don't invoke `/scribe`, `/architect`, `/builder`, `/archivist`, `/deployer`, or `/abzmyan-express` on your own initiative, and don't treat this note as a mandate to route requests through the ticket system — plain conversation and small edits should stay plain conversation and small edits. Only when the user asks for something that's clearly a real feature, bug fix, or refactor — not a question, a trivial edit, or general chat — ask once whether they'd like it run through abzmyan: the standard flow (`/scribe`, then reviewing and approving each stage) for anything worth planning carefully, or `/abzmyan-express "<idea>"` for a one-shot pass on something small (still creates a ticket and updates the index, with one confirmation checkpoint up front instead of a gate at every stage). If they decline or don't engage with the question, just make the change directly — don't ask again unless they bring it up.
